WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.970
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.970
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.530
I'm Kurata Sana, first year junior
high school student.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.280
My manager and driver Rei-kun.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.700
Aoki Award winning Mama and
squirrel Maro-chan.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.250
My best friend who I met in the
bathroom, Fuka.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.130
Mysterious commenting white bat, Babbit.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.250
Babbit started learning the ukulele too. Let's start with C...

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.420
Hayama Akito,
my best friend so that's it.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.260
Leave that guy aside first.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.470
The math video teacher.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.680
I'll give it a shot.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:08.730
Not A Simple Math Video

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.360
Good morning.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.400
Good morning!

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.900
Sana-chan's excited today.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.700
It's the beginning of
the semester.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.990
You can go
home early
on the first
day of the
semester

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.780
That means...

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.080
White dolphin!

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.620
Alright, I'll do my best for the
3rd semester.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.330
Sana, you're excited.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.790
I... l'm full of energy now!

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.460
I want to make achievements.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.420
Could it possibly be Akito told
her his feelings?

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.260
Hey, Sana, what did you do for
New Year's?

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.640
For New Year's?

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.430
I went with Mama and Rei-kun
to the shrine...

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.230
...and rice cake just came up...

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.600
...and then Rei-kun said
something... about FC...

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.900
What? What did the guy say?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.980
So what's with her and Akito now?

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.400
Oh yeah, Hayama came to my house too.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.200
With his dad.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.950
Why the dad?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.780
Hello?

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.030
You're late, Sana-chan!

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.500
You haven't worked in a long time!
You're gonna be late on the first day!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.710
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.870
So bye bye!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.290
See you tomorrow!

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.000
Quick...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.050
Ah, Sana-chan,
wanna eat lunch with us?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.680
Sorry, I have work now so invite me some other day!

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.470
Yo, Hayama!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.970
I'll see you later!

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.220
That girl...

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:34.230
I have my script,
my make-up case and my snack.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.070
I haven't
worked in such long time.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.150
I feel strangely nervous.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:45.620
It's your comeback for work and your first job is some dull role.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.160
It's not dull.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.000
This...

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.330
...is the Studio?!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.210
This is too harsh!
Sana-chan! Let's quit!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.010
Well, well, the most important is
the content of the job.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.170
Ah, wait up!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.260
- Good morning.
- Good morning!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.810
Ah, hey, Sana-chan.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.600
I am the director Karesusukibara.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.890
Nice to meet you.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.350
Kurata Sana here,
nice to meet you.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.440
Hello.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.440
This is the Cameraman and the A.D.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.940
Itou Ichiro, nice to meet you.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.360
Only two?!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.490
Nice to meet you.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.990
- Let's begin.
- Yes.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.580
We wanted you to be in the role
of the math teacher

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.870
but can you do one more little role, act a student?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.920
You see, we didn't have enough
budget so we couldn't hire some of the kids...

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.550
Yeah, we have no money.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.550
What are you talking about?!
Don't joke around!

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.760
I understand, I'll try my best.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.840
Sana-chan.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.260
I'm glad, so let's get started.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:53.770
We've to do it before the sunset.
So we can save studio rent and electrical fee.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.560
Because we have no money.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.650
So let's come and see the set.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:03.110
What... Is Sana-chan's comeback
going to be some poor and dull dirty role?

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.740
Hey, you're infected by that
weird habit.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:07.870
You, young one there.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.740
You have an uneasy look in
your face, but that's alright

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.210
because I've been a cameraman for 40 years

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.290
and I was filming even before
color films.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.260
They used to call color films this.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:27.970
He's a big veteran. He filmed Ishihar
Yutarou and Misora Hibari.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:33.180
I can cook and clean and I'm a
pretty useful A.D. so trust me too.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.140
Y... yes...

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.400
Let's rehearse one of
the student's Nanda-chan's pose...

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.860
...the part where she understands
what the math teacher said.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.150
Ok.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.570
Oh, I see, this is easy easy.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.620
Alright!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.200
Oh, I see! This is easy easy!

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.200
Wow, that's good! Very clever!

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.160
- Is it?
- Really?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.040
Math Teacher is... like this.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.840
I'm the math teacher.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.920
This image is pretty lousy.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.260
Nanda-chan is... like this.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.390
Oh, I see, this is easy easy.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.930
This one is cute.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.930
And how you do it...

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.680
So now let's start with addition.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.520
This is easy easy.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.400
I wonder what 2+2 is.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.440
It's 4, it's easy easy!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.230
Wow, you did very good!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.940
That's weird.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:28.320
Sana-chan's comeback work is
something like this?!

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.320
I agree.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.990
Ok, let's start from the short parts.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.790
From problem 5.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.790
Ok.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.580
If you read the script.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.250
3, 2, 1... 9!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.630
Alright. Q: 5 is a geometry problem.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.210
Nanda-chan,
please read the problem.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.420
Yes!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.640
A trapezoid and parallelo...

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.680
This is bad! It's trapezoid and
parallelogram.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.980
Oh, I see.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:02.980
Trapezoid and Parallelogram

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.440
She read that as that,

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.980
that way is harder.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.490
Wow, an adlib joke,
now that's cool.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.900
Oh no, it's not a joke.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.990
You said something unnecessary again.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.660
Sana-chan, I heard that you were bad at math but I didn't know you couldn't even read it.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.620
It's embarrassing but I'm not
really used it.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.340
I think this problem of whether
she could do math or not happened before.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.510
Let's go.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.260
My new job started! If you would
like you can come and see it!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.680
Sana-chan!

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.390
It's so touching,

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.350
Sana-chan herself gave us
record-mail.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.770
I wonder what kind of job it is.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:49.400
She surprised us with movies and
Broadway,

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.110
I bet it'll be something bigger.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:57.160
Oh, what a wonderful feeling
it is to be invited.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.790
I wonder if that's true.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.160
What is this?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.080
No way, Sana-chan's working here?

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.630
Anyone here?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.260
Oh, Sana-chan is here.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:13.380
But this is too cruel!
It's too cruel!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.930
Sana-chan, why?!

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.850
This is bad, taking so much time.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.770
The sun is going down soon.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.190
Yeah, one light won't do much good because we don't have money.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.570
What is this job?

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.990
Ok, Sana-chan.
Let's do the easiest problem, Q1.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.200
It's be alright with this one, right?

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.700
I'll do my best
with all my strength.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.830
I wonder what happened...
Sana-chan's gloomy.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.960
It's too weird.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.420
Nanda-chan, let's try to solve
this problem.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:48.710
Sure,

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:53.760
47 multiply 67.
First 7 multiply 7 is 49.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:57.010
4 multiply 7... ten of six...

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.600
Cut, cut!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.720
If you do up to that end you're
going to go out of the set.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:02.810
Sorry.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.100
The set is small, and we don't
have money so be careful.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.900
Sana-chan, is possible...
you don't know how to multiply?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.530
Well, I could
manage the first half...

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:17.950
But when it comes to factors of 6
and 7 and 8... well...

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:23.580
It can't be true! A middle school
student Sana can't do multiplication?!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.210
Director! Today, let's stop the multiplication now. We'll go over the rest at home.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.130
So please start from another
problem!

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.590
Start!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.840
Next is division by fraction,

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.050
it seems hard but
it's really easy.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:43.430
Make the fraction that's going to
be divided upside down and multiply.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.640
Yes. Now this one is good.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.650
Ok, Nanda-chan's line.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.610
Oh, I don't get it,
it's all gibberish.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.400
Sana-chan,
that's not in the script.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.280
But I don't know why you flip it,

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.870
and it's division but you multiply.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.540
It's all gibberish.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.540
Sana-chan...

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.210
I don't wanna see this anymore!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.250
Chitose-kun, wait!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:17.880
Anyway, it's not about if Sana-chan
understands or not.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.470
This is acting,

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.760
so act as if you know it, like the
script. Because we don't have money, ok?

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.100
Please! Please!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.690
Yes, Sana-chan, let's just do it.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.650
And it's not that big of a job.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:34.320
But this video is for kids who
aren't really good at math, right?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.700
I'm like that too, and I can't understand, so do the others...

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.570
Oh, Sana-chan. So you're going to
complain with my book again, huh?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.280
Mizoguchi-sensei!

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.410
Sensei,
sorry for coming all this way.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.710
I heard the circumstances,

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.840
seems like you're having
a problem with it.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.130
Yeah, a little.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:55.670
No, it's not a little.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:02.260
Well, Karesusukibara-san, let's
give up for today, and start fresh tomorrow.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.640
Oh but we don't have money so...

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.600
I understand,

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:12.060
but I understand Sana-chan's
reasoning.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:16.530
I'll revise the drama where it's
hard to understand.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.530
Sana took this job at temporary too.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.860
Then she will have time to
practice Nanda-chan's line.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.490
But we don't have money...

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.780
Please.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.240
Sensei.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.830
I understand,
if it means that much to you.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.580
Thank you.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.170
You're actually a pretty good guy.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.130
Ah! What is this?! A bug, a bug!
It's a bug!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:41.970
He didn't change.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.850
Oh well, oh well.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.190
I caused so much trouble.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.560
Mizoguchi-sensei said that...

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.150
So let's work hard tomorrow.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.440
Hey, you still have that weird habit.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:00.820
Sana-chan!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.240
You guys came!

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.160
Ah, where is Chitose-kun?

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.330
He got shocked and went home.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.710
You're not fit for this job,
Sana-chan.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:16.130
It's dull and...

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.630
You don't know what even the
elementary scholars could solve.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:24.260
But you gonna try to teach math.
I think it's impossible.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:29.220
I want you to do something more
pretty and gorgeous.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.230
But not the present job.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:43.570
{parte b}

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.990
Maybe I rush my fences!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:52.080
I wonder if it's impossible for a
person like me to teach math.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.370
Sana-chan,
then do you wanna quit this job?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:01.090
It's a little job... so why don't we take the chance and go to London?

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:04.130
Ah! You mean the one in France?

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.630
London is in England!

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:11.770
Yes, in London you could really
enroll into a prestigious acting school and...

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.520
raise your skills and make a big
roll when you come back!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.560
Eh! I could do that?

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.690
You could do that!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.230
I'll be responsible.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:24.820
So if we go to London with Asako, I'll be with Sana-chan.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.240
So you're only thinking about yourself.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.580
It's not true.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.420
That's not Sana-chan.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:45.380
The real Sana-chan is prettier and
always bright like a sunflower.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:51.180
Yes, days like this... it's not
the real Sana-chan.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.680
It's different.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.850
That has to be...

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.270
London, huh...

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:04.030
I heard London is famous for
acting.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.860
And there are a lot of actors.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.620
It looks like fun to go London
and I don't have to do math.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.370
But it's similar to that
time...

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:22.880
When I couldn't stand watching Hayama and
Fuka together so I ran away to New York.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.840
When I came back it
was the same

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.050
and nothing was solved.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.060
So I really don't know but...

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.100
...I think that if you run away
nothing good is going to happen.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.730
And I also like working a lot.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:44.190
Ah, I can't sum up my thoughts!

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.820
But cross out London,
circle the math video!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.360
So, if that's gonna happen...

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.870
Let's study! Study, study!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:58.750
I give up.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.920
Sana.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:06.050
You always try to do everything
by yourself

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.630
but that's wrong.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.510
When you have a problem,
you beg to god.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.550
When god isn't here,
then you beg to the man.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:17.930
When you have a problem, you have
a friend you can depend on, right?

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.690
Yeah, that's right, Mama.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.980
Yeah, Mama's right.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.320
So Sana, if you choose that, can
you hurry and shut the window?

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.730
Ah, ok.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.530
Ah, Onda-san.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.280
Sensei, what about your deadline?

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.330
Beg to man if god isn't here.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.790
Onda, write it for me.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.160
I can't do that!

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.210
I can't do anything
with these hands.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:41.460
Oh sorry.

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.830
No matter what you say,
I'm not gonna write!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.000
Stop...

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.920
Write your own story.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.960
Deadline, Horrible

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.420
Friend, friend.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.890
At this time, a friend I should
depend on is...

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:56.310
Oh, but it seems they couldn't give help.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.100
Anybody else?

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.640
He looks scary if I ask
something stupid.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.560
Anybody else would do it?

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:08.820
So there is another person,
but I wonder if she will do it.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.070
Leave it to me!

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.320
Well, leave it to you!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:15.200
So with today and tomorrow,

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.990
I'll have to make you understand
these pages, right?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:21.790
Exactly what you said.
Thank you very much.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.330
I'm gonna say this in advance,
but I'm a strict teacher.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.750
Prepare yourself.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:31.050
Thank you, because I am a weakling
who can't even do multiplication.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.050
You can't do multiplication?!

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.590
We're in 7th grade,

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.050
we're doing even harder math,
we're on algebra.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.140
Yes, I'm very sorry.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.020
My math life. I'll sing to you...

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.270
If I think back, in first grade...

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.360
...I did commercial shoots and
skipped school.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.360
Oops I tripped.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.320
...and fell flat on my face in
second grade.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.610
I tumbled through third grade.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.700
Fourth grade was off and splash.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.870
I thought this was bad and tried
to crawl up.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.620
and while I struggled and
struggled,

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.000
...fifth grade math came crashing
down.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.910
And I was back in the pit again.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:05.960
A blub blubbing sixth grade.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.670
I wanna go to a country without
math.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.340
Sensei, can I actually improve?

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.180
Math is a subject that you have to
build one block at a time.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.640
If you have some trouble in the
middle, you must make it clear,

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.140
or you cannot understand at all
day after day.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.890
So you had to give up.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:29.690
But if now you fix that problem
you can't go on ahead at first.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.650
You can catch up to everyone.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:32.820
Really?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.440
Yeah, probably.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:40.910
But the one thing I really don't understand is why we have to study math.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:44.580
What are you saying?!
Now that way of thinking is wrong!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.580
Math is a skill you must have in
order to live life!

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:53.300
To know if the milk in the supermarket is cheap...

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:57.970
If that coat in the supermarket
has a bargain and got cheaper...

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:01.140
If we don't borrow the power of
math we won't know anything!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:04.600
That means we must use math to
drive a hard bargain in everyday life.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.150
Can't you just listen to people
seriously!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.020
Don't eat snacks!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:14.740
So I will
try to help you learn it.

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.360
Fuka-san!

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:20.030
Fuka and Sana work hard together.
Math is life.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.660
Life is math math is life...
if math...

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.160
Fuka, I'm sorry.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
What are you talking about,
we're best friends.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.170
But come to think of it, we're
sitting here together eating snacks.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:31.380
Math... math is life.
It's predestinate.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.090
Math is life.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.920
Life is math. It's predestinate.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.420
The four species, take it easy!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.590
We're good friends all the life.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.220
We'll have splendid life.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:43.390
It'll benefit you all your life
if you learn math.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.390
I'm sorry, Fuka.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.730
You're welcome!
We're good friends!

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:56.360
I found it's the first time to eat
as we walking like this.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.320
With our shocking meeting in the
bathroom on the first day of junior high.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.660
It's cool that we're friends.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:07.580
That time I thought that we looked
like each other.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.670
But our personalities are really
different.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.290
Well, same for grades too.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.840
I wondered what would happen
with Sana and Akito

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.470
but I really don't care about
that anymore.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:23.300
Ah, this is so peaceful.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:27.180
Hold on there, you can't fall
into a peaceful mode this fast!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.690
See, it's the same.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.480
So 4*7 and 7*4 is...

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.070
The same, 28!

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:36.020
That's right.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.110
Oh! I see! Easy easy!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.740
Easy, easy!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:46.700
People who are not good at math
are pretty uneasy about improving in math.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:51.580
And I think everybody wonders why we have to learn this kind of lousy thing.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.460
So I think the video will come out
well if we answer that question.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.090
But...

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.590
That sounds interesting!

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:00.590
Sana-chan,

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:02.970
can you tell me more
of your opinions?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:07.180
But if we do more the time is gonna run out. And we don't have money.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:09.390
We will manage this within
the timeframe.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:12.190
From now on I'll revise my script

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.770
and all we have to do is to film
it all the way.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.820
Now, Sana-chan...

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:22.450
Wasn't Mizoguchi-san only here
to review this job?

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.110
Oh! I see.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:29.160
Yes, but he's actually putting
passion into it. It's weird, isn't it?

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:32.960
If he doesn't call me a bug he's
a pretty good guy.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.670
Mizoguchi-san took most
of Fuka's and my ideas.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.460
And our video subject really
changed.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.510
The filming went along smoothly.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.220
So you guys aren't afraid of math
anymore, right?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:49.010
With this, the math teacher video
volume 1 will end.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.890
Yes, sensei!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:53.100
If you trip then you have to just
wake up again.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.900
And everything will be alright,
so math is life.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.610
Cut! OK!

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.820
Good work, good work!

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.280
It's finally over.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:06.950
Ah, Sana-chan, good work.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.200
Good work.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:11.410
Keep up the good work with
the 2nd volume.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:14.330
Yes, leave it to me!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:18.250
Well, because of Mizoguchi-san, we
got a lot of out opinions in the 1st volume,

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.380
but if the reviews are not good...

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:25.010
I'm afraid the work will be weird
with Sana-chan's opinions added in.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:28.220
I wonder if it'll be alright
because we don't have money.

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:31.350
And Sana-chan got infected too.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.390
The first volume
of math video is finished!

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.220
Anyway...

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:37.810
Mizo-chan, I heard rumors that
you're working on an educational video.

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:41.400
You're the scriptwriter who awes
the audience, why this?

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:44.280
It's because it's a job worthy
enough to do all this work.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:49.530
I wanted to do this job.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.870
I'm home.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:56.210
You look tired. I'll prepared
your dinner at once.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.370
Ok.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.710
Oh yeah, a letter came for you.

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:02.050
I put it there.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.670
Eh, really?

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.010
Oh, this!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:07.930
I wonder if it's a fan letter.
It's been a long time.

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:10.930
What? From Kurata Sana?

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:17.850
I'm Kurata Sana, first year junior
high school student. Nice to meet you.

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:22.730
Rei-kun, what is this?

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:24.400
What's wrote on it?

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:25.820
"You're a fake,

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:28.660
the real Kurata Sana is me."

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.120
What the hell?

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.330
What the matter is it?

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:40.000
matte  mou wakaretai no yo

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:40.000
"Wait... I want us to split up", I said

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.340
ima  KISU wo sorashinagara itta

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.340
Just now, when I turned away from your kiss

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:50.840
Gutto  tsukihanasu kono me ni

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:50.840
Under the gaze of my sharp, firm eyes

